🔹 PART 1 (1.5 Hours) – C# Memory Fundamentals
You are not just learning DS. You are learning how C# behaves internally.

1️⃣ Stack vs Heap

Study This (Conceptually Understand)
	•	What goes on stack?
	•	What goes on heap?
	•	What happens when method is called?
	•	What is call stack?

Example to Try in Visual Studio

class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        int x = 10;
        Person p = new Person();
        p.Age = 30;

        Modify(x, p);

        Console.WriteLine(x);      // ?
        Console.WriteLine(p.Age);  // ?
    }

    static void Modify(int a, Person person)
    {
        a = 50;
        person.Age = 100;
    }
}

class Person
{
    public int Age;
}

Be able to explain:
	•	Why x does not change
	•	Why p.Age changes
	•	Where each variable lives in memory

If you cannot explain memory flow clearly → redo this.

